 "text": "Press Alt+1 for screen-reader mode, Alt+0 to cancel Accessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window D3 Meet Us Services Our Work Blog Careers Contact Us REQUEST A QUOTE Case Study: Farmers Bank of Willards What We Did Digital Ads Search Engine Optimization Multimedia Graphic Design Marketing Print Websites www.fbwbank.com The Story With a 101-year history on Delmarva, Farmers Bank of Willards has a longstanding commitment to the Eastern Shore. Their active involvement in community initiatives, like their 3.21 Race for Down Syndrome Awareness, is as important to them as their dedication to providing the Eastern Shore with a locally focused and trusted financial institution. Farmers Bank of Willards partnered with D3 nearly two years ago to strengthen and modernize its overall marketing strategy. What began with social media, digital advertising, and email marketing has grown into a comprehensive marketing partnership focused on building awareness, engaging the local community, and supporting the bank’s continued growth. As the partnership evolved, D3 also helped refresh the bank’s digital presence, creating a more cohesive experience across its marketing channels. As longtime, locally-based companies, Farmers Bank of Willards and D3 have shared values that helped the two teams quickly establish a foundation of trust. With Farmers Bank of Willards’ deep roots and D3’s tight anchors to the Eastern Shore, we easily understood each other’s audience, priorities, and path forward. Our Journey From the beginning of the partnership, Farmers Bank of Willards and D3 have focused on building a marketing strategy that reflects the bank’s longstanding connection to the Eastern Shore while reaching today’s customers in the places they spend their time. That strategy has included social media, digital advertising, email marketing, SEO, Answer Engine Optimization (AEO), and ongoing content development, all working together to strengthen the bank’s visibility and connect with its communities. As many area banks get bought out by large corporations, Delmarva residents and business owners are searching for a longstanding local bank that’s committed to the Eastern Shore. With so many people and entities in need of a trusted partner, D3 helped Farmers Bank launch its “Switch Kit” to make transitioning accounts simple. Social media has become an important part of that strategy. Through ongoing analytics and performance reviews, D3 and Farmers Bank of Willards have been able to identify what resonates with their audience and build on it. The focus remains on purposeful, community-focused posts that highlight the people, businesses, events, and values that make the Eastern Shore home. Consistent communication has been a key part of the partnership. Regular conversations and team meetings give both teams the opportunity to share ideas, review performance, solve problems, and adjust the strategy as needed. That collaborative approach has allowed the marketing program to evolve alongside the bank and respond to what its customers and communities are looking for. For D3 and Farmers Bank of Willards, staying independently owned does not mean going it alone. Through shared values, open communication, and a commitment to purposeful marketing, the partnership continues to support the bank’s growth while helping it stay connected to the communities it serves. Subscribe Get the latest marketing news and advice. First Name Last Name Email SUBSCRIBE This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply. 12319 Ocean Gateway, Suite 202 Ocean City, Maryland 21842 410-213-2400 212 West Main Street Salisbury, Maryland 21801 Meet Us Testimonials Services Case Studies Videos ID3AS Blog Careers Contact Us Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions Webmail Accessibility Site Map Copyright © 2026 D3. All Rights Reserved. Website Design by D3, Ocean City MD Our Partners PREVIOUS Google YouTube Shopify Amazon Adobe Woocommerce Wordpress Bing Facebook Google YouTube Shopify Amazon Adobe Woocommerce Wordpress Bing Facebook Google NEXT",
